								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=52"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1113.msg11099#msg11099"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1113.msg11099#msg11099">Re: I have no money.</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #16 on:</b> September 13, 2004, 08:28:22 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Everquest actually saves money. EQ offers alot of entertainment a month for less than a couple drinks at the bar. Play EQ more, spend more time at home, spend less on entertainment. Now, only if I could get Taco Bell to deliver.<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
